    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **38 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` as a computed read-only field, following the exact pattern the codebase already uses for other derived fields like `membershipLevel` and `locality`:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` method returning `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `\"PHONE\"` (mirroring the existing `getMembershipLevel()` email check).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression wiring `contactPreference` from `owner.getContactPreference()`, consistent with how `membershipLevel`/`locality` are mapped.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass \u2014 `PHONE` when no email, `EMAIL` when one is present \u2014 and no existing tests regressed.",
